  "location": "2.5 and 2.5",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "azacitidine: 2.5 and 2.5 give different instructions for one patient",
      "summary": "2.5 reads “30-60”. 2.5 reads “15-30”. Example: At bone marrow biopsy cellularity exactly 30%, the table gives two columns, 100% and 50% of the dose. There is no column above 60%. The same text is in 19 labels from 14 labelers in the DailyMed release of 29 October 2026.",
      "impact": "Potential effect on a prescribing decision: medium. Arxo does not say which instruction is correct and gives no dose."
    }
  },
